  (:adr/body "# ADR-2608090800: Industry stack — flagship + craft, parallel waves

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-08-09

## Context

Owner directive: raise industries to flagship maturity and implement fine-grained
process engines like `shirohan`, progressing **all industries in parallel via
subagents**. Two axes must not be conflated:

| Axis | Meaning | Source |
|---|---|---|
| A Flagship product | 7-item checklist (demo/quickstart/freshness/business/demo-field/billing) | ADR-2607122300 / 2607189300 |
| B Craft depth | Deterministic pure `.cljc` process engines | ADR-2608011100 (shirohan), ADR-2607023000 |

Flagship alone yields coordination demos without process truth. Craft alone
yields engines without a governed business face. The industry **stack** is both.

## Decision

### 1. Three parallel lanes per wave

- **Lane A** — flagship generator template on shape-matched ISIC (≤6 repos/wave)
- **Lane B** — wire existing craft into industry actors (≤4)
- **Lane C** — new craft engines (≤3)

Bounded fan-out; independent re-verification; wave failure rate >20% halves fan-out.
No single agent scaffolds the whole fleet. No mock demo HTML. No new GitHub Actions
workflows (fleet-ci). No force-push.

### 2. Resume surfaces

- `90-docs/business/industry-stack-ledger.edn` — append-only, one map per wave
- `90-docs/business/craft-catalog.edn` — craft ↔ isic ↔ surface index

### 3. Wave 0 targets (locked)

- A: sector-diverse no-demo isic (inventory picks)
- B1: shirohan → isic-1313 prepress ops
- B2: inkan → best-fit document/legal isic
- C1: `seihan` paper prepress craft (boundary vs shirohan)
- C2: isic-1410 blueprint → minimal `:implemented` (pattern craft later)

### 4. Craft invariants (from shirohan)

Coordinates/quantities are not LLM-owned. Unreadable input must produce findings.
Writer/reader separation for exports. DADS UI on itonami.cloud surfaces.

## Consequences

Parallel waves replace serial single-industry perfectionism. Quality is enforced by
gates and spot re-verification, not by batch size=1 forever. OS connect
(ADR-2608070000) and maturity-improve (ADR-2608080000) remain separate programs —
stack work may feed them but does not replace their ticks.
")
  (:adr/decision-summary "{:axes [:flagship :craft], :lanes [:A :B :C], :wave0 true, :ledger industry-stack-ledger.edn}")))
